const supplementarySections = {
  'mobile-app-development-company-delhi': [['Agree how product changes are reviewed','Mobile projects often require decisions from product, design and business stakeholders. Choose who can resolve open questions, how consolidated feedback will be shared and what happens when a requested change affects the agreed scope. Set review points around complete user journeys so feedback considers the flow from start to finish. The exact review process belongs in the project plan, not in an assumed delivery promise.']],
  'shopify-development-company-delhi': [['Clarify ownership before store handover','Confirm who controls the store account, provider accounts, product data and brand materials. Identify what the business team needs to update themselves and which parts should be documented at handover. Record any agreed post-launch work separately. These decisions help the store remain manageable after the development engagement and make responsibilities clear without implying that a particular training or support package is automatically included.']],
  'flutter-app-development-company-india': [['Keep platform details in the project brief','List device permissions, notifications, deep links, accessibility needs and any behaviour that differs between Android and iOS. Some requirements may affect the architecture or test approach even when most of the code is shared. Identify who will provide developer accounts and release content. The project can then include those responsibilities and technical questions explicitly rather than treating release as a final click.']],
  'ai-chatbot-development-company-india': [['Define a safe fallback for requests outside scope','Write examples of questions the chatbot should not answer and the response it should give in those cases. Decide whether it should request clarification, explain the boundary or direct the user to a person. Review how the fallback works with the intended audience and source content. This is a planning requirement; the actual handover channel and operating process must be confirmed before an implementation commitment is made.']],
  'website-development-cost-delhi': [['Plan requirements in reviewable groups','A website brief can group work into page templates, content, interactions, integrations and launch checks. For each group, identify what the business will supply and what the development scope should cover. Review one representative page and one core workflow before assuming every page is identical. This helps surface differences early, such as unique content structure or a special form, and makes the discussion more precise without inventing a standard package.'],['Estimate content and migration work clearly','List pages and assets that must move from an existing website, if there is one. Identify whether copy and images are approved, whether old URLs need to remain available and what content requires a new structure. Ask how redirects and content checks are treated in a proposal. These tasks can change the scope even when the new site appears visually similar, so they should be described and agreed rather than left implicit. Before requesting an estimate, prepare a page inventory and mark content as ready, in progress or not yet supplied. Note who can approve copy and images, and gather access or export details for an existing platform if migration is being considered. This lets the scoping discussion distinguish development tasks from missing business inputs and avoids assuming that content production or data migration is included.']],
  'app-development-cost-india': [['Separate a build estimate from recurring operating costs','Ask which costs relate to project design and development, and which may recur through hosting, third-party providers, store accounts or ongoing maintenance. Provider charges depend on the chosen services and business usage, so they should be confirmed from those providers rather than guessed. Make clear who owns each account and who will handle renewals or operational work. Techverse AI has not supplied numerical app prices for this guide; the goal is to prepare a requirements-based estimate request.'],['Describe first release acceptance in advance','Write down the user journeys, devices and behaviours that define an acceptable first release. Include validation, error cases, permissions, responsive or platform-specific details and any agreed integrations. Name the person who can approve the completed work and how issues will be recorded. This does not create a one-size-fits-all test plan; it helps make delivery expectations and review effort visible in the estimate.'],['Ask for assumptions and exclusions in writing','An estimate should identify assumptions about supplied designs, content, accounts, external APIs and access to existing systems. Ask which items are excluded, what information could change the estimate and how new requests will be handled after scope is agreed. Clarifying these points makes proposals easier to compare and helps the business budget for decisions it still needs to make. No Techverse price range is published here until the owner confirms one.'],['Prepare technical information for discovery','If an app will use an existing service or data source, collect its documentation, access owner and known constraints. If the project needs new user roles or several release platforms, write down each requirement and how it affects the first version. Share design files or interface examples if they exist, and identify decisions that remain open. Complete information does not guarantee a fixed estimate, but it helps the team identify unknowns and explain what needs further investigation before agreeing scope.']]
};

